al output). Verified in both modes, including running both binaries under a real PTY (byte-identical).\n\n**C quirks preserved, not \"fixed\":** `bad()` does *not* call `helperBad()` — so `helperGood()` appears in the output and `helperBad()` never does. `helper_bad` is kept defined and uncalled. `printLine`'s `NULL` guard is unreachable (all 8 call sites pass literals), so no test can cover it; I documented that instead of inventing a test that pretends to.\n\n## Gate status\n\n- Both build clean — 0 warnings, 0 errors (from a wiped `target/`)\n- `cargo test`: **25 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored**, in both debug and `--release`\n- Nothing `#[ignore]`d or skipped (grep-verified: 0 markers)\n- `c_src/` unmodified — sources retain original timestamps; only the required `c_src/build/` was added\n\nOne caveat on coverage honesty: `stdout_to_dev_full_matches` early-returns if `/dev/full` is absent. On this Linux host it did execute the real comparison, but on a platform lacking `/dev/full` it would silently pass without testing anything. `strace` was also blocked by the sandbox, so the syscall-pattern claim in Bug 2 rests on the PTY and pipe comparisons rather than direct syscall counts."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":48372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":540,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82e3f9e1-c2cf-409e-9843-c19d761a5707","uuid":"9f5c60b0-7be5-4044-8003-d40faf387bd7","timestamp":"2026-08-28T12:32:34.796Z"}
